## Built-in apps — the non-game tiles (OmniOS.md §17, §18).
## Existing, proven programs rather than ones written here.
## mpv plays video and music; thunar browses drives. thunar-volman and gvfs
## are what make removable media actually work in Thunar, which is the whole
## reason it is here. Comments stay on their own lines: the rest of this file
## does the same, and it avoids depending on how mkarchiso strips trailing ones.
mpv
chromium
thunar
thunar-volman
gvfs
ffmpegthumbnailer

## The store, and what a tile menu needs to manage what it installed.
##
## gnome-software is Ubuntu's store — the same program, before Canonical
## renamed it. Arch builds it without the PackageKit plugin, so its catalogue
## is Flathub rather than the repositories, which is the right choice here: a
## Flatpak carries its own libraries, so installing one cannot drag the base
## system into the partial upgrade that "pacman -Sy something" invites.
##
## archlinux-appstream-data is what makes it look like a store rather than a
## package list — names, summaries and icons for anything shown from the repos.
## xdg-desktop-portal-gtk is already pulled in by the file manager and is what
## lets a sandboxed app open a file dialog at all.
## checkupdates (pacman-contrib) keeps "check for update" safe on native
## packages: it compares against a throwaway database instead of running
## pacman -Sy, which on Arch leaves the system one partial upgrade from a
## mismatched libc.
gnome-software
flatpak
archlinux-appstream-data
pacman-contrib

## A Flatpak install is a privileged operation and polkit is what authorises it.
## The rule in /etc/polkit-1/rules.d grants it without a prompt, but an agent is
## still needed for anything the rule does not cover, and a console with no
## agent simply fails silently instead of asking.
hyprpolkitagent

## Branding — Phase 11
plymouth
ttf-dejavu
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji

## Controllers. multilib ships no lib32 SDL2 of any kind; lib32-sdl3 is the
## only 32-bit SDL there, and sdl2-compat serves the SDL2 API on top of SDL3.
## game-devices-udev is AUR-only and lives in packages.aur.txt.
sdl2-compat
sdl3
lib32-sdl3
